menu "PCB2 board"

choice PCB2_MICROPHONE
    prompt "Populated microphone (pin 2 tied to GND)"
    default PCB2_MIC_ZTS6672
    help
        Select the actual fitted part, rather than the schematic library name.
        ZTS6672 DS-13 specifies the right I2S slot with SELECT low and CONFIG
        open. ICS-43434 uses the left slot with LR low. This setting does not
        change the shared speaker I2S clocks or format.

config PCB2_MIC_ZTS6672
    bool "ZillTek ZTS6672"

config PCB2_MIC_ICS43434
    bool "TDK ICS-43434 (LR low; left slot)"

endchoice

config PCB2_MIC_RIGHT_SLOT
    bool "Read right microphone slot at startup"
    default n
    help
        The tested PCB currently provides nonzero data only in the left slot.
        ZTS6672 DS-13 specifies right with SELECT low and CONFIG open, so its
        actual mode/pin state still needs checking. Override this for a board
        confirmed to drive right. The keypad diagnostic selector can switch
        slots temporarily without changing clocks or reflashing.

endmenu
